  data: {
    LLM: "In the early betting rounds, look for 'connected' hole cards. If you have a Jack and 10, any path with a King, Queen, or 9 becomes highly valuable.\n\nCenter Card Weight: The center card is the most powerful because it's the only one that completes both possible paths. If you have 'outside' matches early, you are heavily dependent on that center card.\n\nPot Odds: Since the community cards are revealed slowly, calculate your 'outs' for each of the two potential paths. A hand that is weak on the horizontal row might be a monster on the vertical.",
    Player: "In the early betting rounds, look for 'connected' hole cards. If you have a Jack and 10, any path with a King, Queen, or 9 becomes highly valuable.\n\nCenter Card Weight: The center card is the most powerful because it's the only one that completes both possible paths. If you have 'outside' matches early, you are heavily dependent on that center card.\n\nPot Odds: Since the community cards are revealed slowly, calculate your 'outs' for each of the two potential paths. A hand that is weak on the horizontal row might be a monster on the vertical.",
